  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/organism-esmfold-P81459-esmatlas-run> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "ESMFold prediction run for Cytochrome c from Thunnus alalunga (P81459), with its input and output checksums" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/organism-esmfold-P81459-esmatlas-run> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Input: UniProt P81459, sequence version 1, residues 1-103, 103 aa; the vendored record is organism-design/esmfold/inputs/P81459.json (SHA-256 5fa3d4a6479ff261d57edf250d8f1f54c06890e47bd3023bcd787e15789909a5) and the sequence SHA-256 is e1be091fd55caa18322581452442a003ee72fdeb02e33cc6e7c35b80742e709f. Call: POST to https://api.esmatlas.com/foldSequence/v1/pdb/ on 2026-10-31T06:41:36.655Z, HTTP 200, 0.1 s. The service reports its own version as \"ESMFOLD V1 PREDICTION FOR INPUT (PDB TITLE record)\". Output: one predicted structure, 103 residues modelled, written to P81459-esmatlas/predicted.pdb (SHA-256 3dd82c626b2b6a564343ae1b199ca28fb8d26f80eb2a98eef8ce1992fa4e592f). Every pLDDT number below was read from the B-factor column of that file; the file carries the scale \"0-1, multiplied by 100 here\". Mean 93, minimum 83, maximum 96, fraction at or above 70 is 1, fraction at or above 90 is 0.893. The run record is organism-design/esmfold/runs/P81459-esmatlas/result.json (SHA-256 ceba59ba768165f578179d2920dd826917b8e9fb95c25f28e3d6099057bec908)." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/organism-esmfold-P81459-esmatlas-run> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "organism-design/esmfold/runs/P81459-esmatlas/result.json" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/organism-esmfold-P81459-esmatlas-run> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "sha256:ceba59ba768165f578179d2920dd826917b8e9fb95c25f28e3d6099057bec908" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/organism-esmfold-P81459-esmatlas-run> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> <https://www.uniprot.org/uniprotkb/P81459> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/organism-esmfold-P81459-esmatlas-run> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://api.esmatlas.com/foldSequence/v1/pdb/> .
